{
  "table_id": "Table_S16",
  "display_number": "S16",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S16. Four-group adjusted BAA contrasts and difference-in-differences interaction estimates",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Adjusted contrasts are from linear mixed-effects models with participant-level random intercepts, inverse-probability weights, and robust standard errors. The O₃ within high EVI contrast is the difference between the High EVI/high O₃ and High EVI/low O₃ groups. The difference-in-differences (DiD) interaction estimates departure from additivity of mean BAA differences and should not be interpreted as evidence that EVI offsets, attenuates, or causally reverses O₃-related BAA. Abbreviations: BAA, biological age acceleration; DiD, difference-in-differences; EVI, enhanced vegetation index; O₃, ozone."
  ],
